; DOMAIN: mordell-weil [CLOSED, derived 2026-07-25]
; Claim: The Mordell-Weil theorem states that for an elliptic curve E over Q (more generally over a number field K), the group of rational points E(Q) is a finitely generated abelian group: E(Q) = Z^r (+) E(Q)_tors, where r >= 0 is the rank and E(Q)_tors is the finite torsion subgroup. The proof has two parts: (1) the Weak Mordell-Weil theorem, E(Q)/mE(Q) is finite (proven via Galois cohomology / descent, embedding into the Selmer group); (2) the theory of heights — the canonical Neron-Tate height h-hat is a positive-definite quadratic form on E(Q) tensor R, and the descent argument via h-hat with the finiteness of E(Q)/mE(Q) forces finite generation (infinite descent / Fermat descent). The rank r is exactly the quantity bounded above by the m-Selmer group, and its precise value is the subject of BSD.
; Bridge: genesis_elliptic_curve (E(Q) is the Mordell-Weil group of rational points of the elliptic curve, an abelian group under the chord-tangent law) + genesis_selmer_group (weak Mordell-Weil embeds E(Q)/p^n into Sel_{p^n}, so the Selmer group provides the finiteness of E(Q)/mE(Q) and the rank bound) + genesis_group_cohomology (the descent map E(Q)/mE(Q) -> H^1(G_Q, E[m]) is a Galois-cohomology Kummer sequence, the cohomological engine of weak Mordell-Weil).
(= (mordell-weil-group $E) (rational-points $E (Q)))
(= (finitely-generated $E) (iso (mordell-weil-group $E) (direct-sum (free-abelian (rank $E)) (torsion-subgroup $E))))
(= (weak-mw $E $m) (finite (quotient (mordell-weil-group $E) (mult-by $m (mordell-weil-group $E)))))
(= (descent-embedding $E $m) (inject (quotient (mordell-weil-group $E) (mult-by $m)) (selmer $E $p $n)))
(= (canonical-height $E) (neron-tate-height $E))
(= (height-positive-definite $E) (positive-definite (canonical-height $E) (tensor (mordell-weil-group $E) (R))))
(= (rank-bounded-by-selmer $E) (leq (rank $E) (selmer-rank $E)))
(= (mw-proof $E $m) (infinite-descent (weak-mw $E $m) (canonical-height $E)))